WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.584
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit
1: Languages and Communication.

2
00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:10.778
The theme is languages and communication:
how ideas travel, how rumours outrun facts,

3
00:00:10.858 --> 00:00:14.786
and how careful readers and listeners separate the two.

4
00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:20.834
You will read two information texts about
how rumours spread and how to check them,

5
00:00:20.914 --> 00:00:28.922
then follow Amal and Nora through the story Whispers
Beyond the Gate as a hoax flyer sweeps their harbour city.

6
00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:36.938
The grammar focus covers contrast conjunctions (although,
while, whereas), -ing forms as subjects and objects,

7
00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:44.517
the present continuous, abstract nouns, reported
speech, conditionals, connectives and multi-word verbs.

8
00:00:44.597 --> 00:00:51.731
Along the way you will learn thirty-one new words,
write a contrast paragraph and an opinion essay,

9
00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:55.156
and argue a case aloud for five to six minutes.

10
00:00:55.236 --> 00:01:01.277
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:01:01.357 --> 00:01:03.124
By the end of this unit,

12
00:01:03.204 --> 00:01:11.356
you will be able to summarise the central ideas and
important details in Languages and Communication texts.

13
00:01:11.436 --> 00:01:17.280
You will also support inferences and
comparisons with relevant text evidence.

14
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.973
You will also use Grade 8 vocabulary
accurately in discussion and writing.

15
00:01:23.053 --> 00:01:25.820
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:32.752
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
concise, barricade, zeal, longevity, definition, allot.

17
00:01:32.832 --> 00:01:38.312
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:38.392 --> 00:01:42.636
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:42.716 --> 00:01:49.576
The reading sequence includes The Speed of a Whisper:
How Rumours Travel and The Fact-Checker's Toolkit.

20
00:01:49.656 --> 00:01:50.511
Read actively.

21
00:01:50.591 --> 00:01:55.115
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:55.195 --> 00:01:59.453
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:05.012
The first language focus is Contrast
Conjunctions: Although, While and Whereas.

24
00:02:05.092 --> 00:02:13.455
Although, while and whereas are contrast conjunctions: they
join two clauses that express different or surprising ideas,

25
00:02:13.535 --> 00:02:19.507
showing that both things can be true at the
same time even when they seem to conflict.

26
00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:27.177
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:27.257 --> 00:02:31.374
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Contrast Debate.

28
00:02:31.454 --> 00:02:36.140
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.768
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:43.539
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:45.324
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:45.404 --> 00:02:53.010
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.737
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:56.817 --> 00:03:05.355
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
